(1) $\mathbf{E}[X(f)\mathrm{e}^{-X(g)}] = \mu (f\mathrm{e}^{-g})\mathbf{E}[\mathrm{e}^{-X(g)}]$;
(2) $\mathbf{E}[X(f)^2\mathrm{e}^{-X(g)}] = [\mu (f^2\mathrm{e}^{-g}) + \mu (f\mathrm{e}^{-g})^2 ]\mathbf{E}[\mathrm{e}^{-X(g)}];$
(3) $\mathbf{E}[\tilde{X}(f)^4] = \mu(f^4) + 3\mu(f^2)^2.$
